WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.644
Order matters. The wrong way: pick the highest-affinity pair, then check the capacity.

2
00:00:10.644 --> 00:00:19.222
At step two of G01 at capacity 2, the largest, AB–C, is over capacity, so it stops at 4 clusters, cut 13.

3
00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:26.244
The right way filters first: D–E can still merge, and it stops at 3 clusters, cut 8.

4
00:00:26.244 --> 00:00:29.711
Same graph; only the order differs.

5
00:00:30.111 --> 00:00:38.022
Three twin rooms: every node has size 2, capacity 3, K = 2. The bound is 2; nothing is ruled out.

6
00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:43.711
Yet any two together make 4, over 3: at least 3 clusters.

7
00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:50.511
Meeting the bound is not feasibility. Deciding whether it fits is bin packing itself.

8
00:00:50.911 --> 00:00:55.378
How costly is exhaustive search? Ways to group n nodes:

9
00:00:55.378 --> 00:01:00.844
5 nodes, 52; 10 nodes, already over a hundred thousand.

10
00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:05.644
15 and 20 nodes quickly reach tens of trillions.

11
00:01:05.644 --> 00:01:11.444
So this course uses exhaustive search only as a check at 10 nodes or fewer.

12
00:01:11.844 --> 00:01:18.200
On greedy_trap, greedy stops at 3 clusters, cut 8.

13
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.222
The feasible two-cluster plan AC | BD has cut 10.

14
00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:28.467
Greedy's cut is smaller, because it has one more cluster.

15
00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:32.600
Compare cuts only at the same number of clusters.

16
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:39.800
How far off can a legal greedy result be? Scale the suboptimal graph.

17
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.044
M = 10: 18 versus 11.

18
00:01:43.044 --> 00:01:46.956
M = 100: 198 versus 101.

19
00:01:46.956 --> 00:01:51.533
M = 1000: 1998 versus 1001.

20
00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:57.667
Greedy is 2(M − 1), optimal M + 1: the gap approaches twice.

21
00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:04.422
With every size 1, capacity 3 gives ABC | DE, cut 3.

22
00:02:04.422 --> 00:02:10.333
Change only A to 2, and the result becomes AB | CDE, cut 5.

23
00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:16.022
Real cells differ in area; capacity must count the sum of areas.

24
00:02:16.422 --> 00:02:18.489
Six things to keep.

25
00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:35.844
Next: nodes don't merge; they change labels.
